From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:51:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tile SVG background images, and draw SVGs that use filters
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An SVG background image was drawn once, whatever `background-repeat` and
`background-size` said; a raster one tiles. It now tiles the same way, a
tile per repeat, as gradients do (past 1024 tiles only the first row is
drawn, so a tiny tile over a large area doesn't encode the tree
thousands of times).

SVG filters (`feTurbulence`, `feGaussianBlur`, `feColorMatrix`, …) aren't
drawn by the vector path (anyrender_svg), so a filtered shape came out
as a plain black fill: a paper-grain texture was a black square. An SVG
image whose tree uses filters is now rasterised with resvg at the size it
is drawn and cached by source and size (16 sizes), then drawn as an
image, for background images and `<img>` alike; others stay vectors.

Tests in `background_svg_tiling.rs`.
